/	LAST EDIT: 22-MAY-2014 CJL.

/	TAKEN FROM A 1978 P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE IMAGE [KNOWN TO NOT BE A FINAL RELEASE].

/	THIS IS THE ACTUAL IMAGE OF BLOCK 0060 OF A P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE.  BLOCK 0060 IS
/	RESERVED AS THE "FILE" TO BE PASSED TO THE SLURP LOADER LAST IF THE /I SWITCH
/	IS PASSED TO THE "BIN" UTILITY WHEN INVOKED TO LOAD BINARY FILES.

/	SUCCESSFUL OPERATION DEPENDS ON THIS "FILE" BEING THE LAST FILE DESCRIPTOR IN
/	THE FILE LIST.  MOST OF THE CODING IS LOADED OVER THE SYSTEM FILE AREA
/	[07757-07777] SINCE AT THE POINT THIS "FILE" BEING LOADED, THE FORMER CONTENTS
/	OF ARE MEANINGLESS.  ONCE THE CODE IS COMPLETELY LOADED, THE SLURP LOADER IS
/	OVERLAID TO PASS CONTROL TO THE JUST-LOADED CODE.

/	THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE SYSTEM HANDLER IS OPERATIONAL IF ALL ADDRESSES FROM
/	SBOOT [7600] THROUGH SADDR [7746] ARE LOADED.  THE REST OF THE PAGE NEED NOT
/	BE LOADED FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER TO COMPLETELY FUNCTION; SYSTEM RESTART
/	AT 07600 WILL BE OPERATIONAL.

/	MORE IMPORTANTLY, BY AVOIDING OVERLAYING THE REST OF THE PAGE, THE CODE IN
/	CONTROL IS NOT OVERLAID.  THE ORIGINAL STARTUP INFORMATION PASSED TO THE SLURP
/	LOADER IS ALSO INTACT ALLOWING STARTUP AT THE INTENDED ADDRESS AND FIELD.

/	TO END THE TAPE OPERATION RELOADING THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER FROM BLOCK 0000,
/	REFERENCE CAN BE MADE TO VARIOUS CONSTANTS WITHIN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.
/	A CONSTANT 0200 IS REQUIRED TO STOP THE TAPE; IT IS AVAILABLE WITHIN THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CODE JUST READ IN.

/	OPERATIONAL CHANGES DUE TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER OVERLAYING THE SLURP
/	LOADER.

/	THE ONLY INTERNAL CHANGE IS THE EXACT VALUE OF THE DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS
/	USED WHEN NONE IS SPECIFIED ON THE COMMAND-LINE.  A NEW SAFE HALT DEFAULT
/	LOCATION IS DEFINED WITHIN THE CODE READ INTO THE SYSTEM FILE AREA.
/	ADDITIONALLY, A JMP BACK TO THE SAFE HALT IS INCLUDED IN CASE THE USER PRESSES
/	"CONTINUE" ON THE FRONT PANEL OF THE CPU.  THE "BIN" UTILITY CHANGES THE
/	DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS FROM THAT OF THE SLURP LOADER TO THE SAFE HALT
/	ADDRESS DEFINED HERE; ONCE-ONLY INITIALIZATION OF THE "BIN" UTILITY HANDLES
/	ALL CASES.

/	WHEN THE USER PROGRAM IS LOADED AND STARTED, THE NET EFFECT IS THAT THE SYSTEM
/	DEVICE HANDLER IS ALSO RESIDENT IN MEMORY.  THE EQUIVALENT RESULTS WOULD HAVE
/	BEEN ACHIEVED USING THE VIRTUAL LOADER; HOWEVER, THE OVERHEAD OF THE VIRTUAL
/	LOADER HAS BEEN ELIMINATED.  THE LOADING PROCESS IS NOTICEABLY FASTER; THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE CAN REMAIN WRITE-LOCKED UNLESS THE USER PROGRAM REQUIRES ACCESS
/	TO WRITE OPERATIONS OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.  [NOTE: THE SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER RECOVERS FROM ANY DEVICE ERROR.  AS SUCH, THE USER CAN ENABLE WRITING
/	LATER, WHERE APPROPRIATE, TO HARMLESSLY RECOVER FROM ANY FORM OF SYSTEM DEVICE
/	ERROR SUCH AS WRITE-LOCK.]
/	THE "GET" COMMAND CAN USE EITHER THE OVERALL METHOD DESCRIBED HERE OR SPECIFY
/	THE /V OPTION TO INVOKE THE VIRTUAL LOADER.  THE PERMANENT CONTENTS OF BLOCK
/	0000 ARE IDENTICAL TO WHAT THE VIRTUAL LOADER SETS UP IN THE SYSTEM LOADER
/	AREA [TO SAVE ALL USER MEMORY AND THEN RESTART THE SYSTEM].  [NOTE: THE
/	INTERNAL OPERATIONS OF THE VIRTUAL LOADER INCLUDE CALLS PLACED IN THE SYSTEM
/	LOADER REPLACING THE DEFAULT VALUES.  SINCE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS NEVER
/	DISPLACED WHEN THE VIRTUAL LOADER IS IN EFFECT, ONE OF THE LAST ACTIONS OF THE
/	VIRTUAL LOADER IS TO RESTORE THE SYSTEM LOADER TO ITS DEFAULT CONTENTS.]  THIS
/	ENSURES THAT STARTING THE PROGRAM AT 07632 WILL PERFORM THE MEMORY SAVE
/	OPERATION AND THEN RESTART THE SYSTEM.  [NOTE: "GET" IS ACTUALLY AN ALTERNATE
/	ENTRY INTO THE "BIN" PROGRAM THAT FORCES APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE SWITCHES;
/	"BIN" CAN BE INVOKED WITH THE IDENTICAL OPTIONS EXPLICITLY GIVEN; HOWEVER,
/	THESE OPTIONS ARE NOT FORCES AS IN THE "GET" COMMAND.]

/	WHEN THE /I SWITCH IS GIVEN CAUSING THE LOADING OF THIS "FILE", THE OVERALL
/	MAXIMUM USER-SPECIFIED FILE COUNT DROPS FROM SEVENTEEN TO SIXTEEN.

/	KNOWN LIMITATIONS.

/	THE ONCE-ONLY CODE OF THE "BIN" UTILITY REQUIRES SOME REWORK TO PREVENT
/	ATTEMPTS AT IMPOSSIBLE COMMANDS.  IF THE /I SWITCH IS GIVEN, AN ERROR MESSAGE
/	SHOULD BE ISSUED IF EXACTLY SEVENTEEN FILES ARE SUPPLIED BY THE USER.
/	PRESENTLY, IN THE SPECIFIC RELEASE REFERENCED, THE SEVENTEENTH FILE IS MERELY
/	IGNORED.  THIS CAN EASILY BE CORRECTED IN A FUTURE RELEASE OF EITHER P?S/8 OR
/	THE "BIN" UTILITY.

/	THIS VERSION OF THE /I "FILE" DOES NOT SUPPORT MULTIPLE LOGICAL UNITS FOR THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE.  THE TC01/TC08 CAN SUPPORT A SPECIAL SUPERSET BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE
/	TO ALLOW BOOTUP TO A SYSTEM ON A LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT OTHER THAN 0.  THIS CODE
/	MUST BE UPGRADED TO MAINTAIN FULL COMPATIBILITY.

/	TO ACCOMPLISH THIS, THE CODE CAN BE REWORKED TO OVERLAY ADDITIONAL AREAS OF
/	THE SLURP LOADER THAT CAN BE DESTROYED WHILE THE LOADING OF THIS CODE IS IN
/	EFFECT.  FOR EXAMPLE, THIS CODE IS TOTALLY LOCATED WITHIN A SINGLE DECTAPE
/	BLOCK.  PART OF THE SLURP LOADER CODING IS CONCERNED WITH ADDITIONAL BLOCK
/	TRANSFERS; A TYPICAL BINARY TFS FILE CONTAINS UP TO SIXTEEN BLOCKS.  SUCH
/	SECTIONS OF CODE ARE NO LONGER NEEDED WHEN THIS CODE IS IN CONTROL.  THUS,
/	SOME ADDITIONAL WORDS OF THIS "FILE" CODE MIGHT BE LOCATED OVER THE STATED 
/	PORTION OF THE [NO LONGER NEEDED] SLURP LOADER CODING.

/	PORTIONS OF THE BOOTSTRAP CODE WITHIN THE SLURP LOADER ARE USED BY THIS CODE;
/	HOWEVER, MUCH OF IT IS NOT; THIS WOULD ALSO ALLOW POTENTIAL LENGTHENING OF
/	THIS "FILE" TO ACCOMMODATE ADDITIONAL FEATURES.
/	DEFINED SYMBOLS.

/	NOTE: OTHER THAN THE SLURP CONTROL DEFINITIONS, THE REST OF THE DEFINITIONS ON
/	THIS PAGE HAVE BEEN TAKEN FROM OTHER P?S/8 SOURCE FILES TO ALLOW THIS CODE TO
/	BE ASSEMBLED AS AN INDEPENDENT SOURCE CODE FILE.  GENERALLY ALL COMPONENTS OF
/	THE TC01/TC08 OVERALL SUPPORT ARE COMBINED TOGETHER WHEN P?S/8 IS BEING
/	CREATED.

/	P?S/8 SYSTEM DEFINITIONS.

	SBOOT=	7600			/SYSTEM REBOOT ADDRESS
	SFILES=	7757			/PASSED FILE LIST STARTS HERE
	SLOAD=	7632			/SYSTEM LOADER ADDRESS

/	P?S/8 TC01/TC08 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER DEFINITIONS.

	S200=	7602			/CONSTANT 0200
	SADDR=	7746			/LATEST TRANSFER ADDRESS

/	SLURP LOADER DEFINITIONS.

	SLPSTRT=7626			/SLURP LOADER NEXT FILE ADDRESS
	SLUSTRT=7746			/SLURP LOADER PROGRAM START ADDRESS
	SLWAIT=	7613			/SLURP BOOTSTRAP WAIT ROUTINE
	SL220=	7637			/CONSTANT 0220
	SL600=	7607			/CONSTANT 0600
	SL7577=	7623			/CONSTANT 7577

/	SLURP CONTROL DEFINITIONS.
	DA=	0			/DATA WORD	
	EF=	1			/END-OF-FILE
	FL=	3			/FIELD SETTING
	OR=	2			/ORIGIN SETTING

/	TC01/TC08 DECTAPE DEFINITIONS.

	CA=	7755			/CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK
	DTCA=	6762			/CLEAR STATUS REGISTER "A"
	DTLA=	6766			/LOAD STATUS REGISTER "A" FROM AC, CLEAR AC
	DTLB=	6774			/AC[6-8] TO BREAK FIELD, CLEAR AC
	DTRA=	6761			/STATUS REGISTER "A" .OR. INTO AC
	DTRB=	6772			/STATUS REGISTER "B" .OR. INTO AC
	DTSF=	6771			/SKIP ON DECTAPE FLAG OR ERROR FLAG SET
	DTXA=	6764			/AC .XOR. INTO STATUS REGISTER "A", CLEAR AC
	WC=	7754			/WORD COUNT REGISTER FOR 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK
/	THE "FILE" IMAGE REQUIRES AN AVAILABLE BUFFER WHEN THE SYSTEM IS BEING
/	CREATED.

/	SINCE IT IS READ IN ONE WORD AT A TIME BY THE SLURP LOADER, THE INTERNAL
/	ORIGIN WILL BE SET ACCORDINGLY FOR ASSEMBLY PURPOSES.  THE BUFFER ADDRESS IS
/	ONLY USED WHEN THE SYSTEM IS GENERATED [OR SOME EQUIVALENT SYSTEM
/	RECONFIGURATION UTILITY EVENTUALLY WRITTEN TO SIMPLIFY THE PROCESS].

	*7200				/BUFFER ADDRESS FOR SYSTEM GENERATION PURPOSES.

	RELOC	SBOOT			/PAGE WHERE EVERYTHING HAPPENS.

/	NOTE: THIS IS AN IMAGE OF A VALID [SHORT] SLURP FILE; HOWEVER, IT DOES NOT
/	INCLUDE AN ORIGIN TO 0200 AS IS USUALLY THE CASE.  [AS SUCH, WERE IT AN ACTUAL
/	TFS BINARY FILE, CERTAIN UTILITIES COULD REJECT IT AS INVALID.  SINCE IT IS
/	ALWAYS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0060, NO FILE SYSTEM ACCESS EXISTS.]

	FL^4+OR^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA	/CONTROL WORD.

	CDF	00			/FIELD SETTING TO FIELD 0.
	
	SFILES				/*SFILES

	RELOC	SFILES			/WHERE THIS ASSEMBLES.

/	WHEN CONTROL IS PASSED TO HERE, START THE BLOCK 0000 RELOADING PROCESS.

SLIGO,	TAD	SL600/(600)		/GET REWIND BITS.
	JMS	SLWAIT			/WAIT FOR THE TAPE TO REWIND.
	TAD	SL7577/(SBOOT-1)	/SETUP THE
	DCA	CA			/CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.

	DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA	/CONTROL WORD.

	RELOC	.-1			/RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.

	TAD	TRNLEN/(SBOOT-SADDR)	/GET WORD COUNT VALUE TO TRANSFER JUST
					/ENOUGH OF THE SYSTEM HANDLER NEEDED.
	DCA	WC			/SETUP THE WORD COUNT REGISTER.
	TAD	SL220/(220)		/GET READ FORWARD COMMAND BITS.
	DTLA				/START READING BLOCK 0000.
	DTSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA^4+DA	/CONTROL WORD.

	RELOC	.-1			/RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.

/	AT THIS POINT, [MOST OF] BLOCK 0000 IS READ IN.  WE CAN ACCESS CONSTANTS
/	LOCATED WITHIN THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.

	TAD	S200/(200)		/GET MOTION BIT.
	DTXA				/STOP THE TAPE.
	JMP	SLUSTRT			/GO START THE USER PROGRAM.

TRNLEN,	SBOOT-SADDR			/DESIRED TRANSFER LENGTH

	ZBLOCK	1			/EMPTY SPACE.

/	THIS IS THE DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS OF A SAFE HALT.

DEFADR,	HLT				/DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS.

	DA^4+OR^4+DA^4+EF^4+EF^4+EF	/CONTROL WORD.

	RELOC	.-1			/RESET ASSEMBLY ADDRESS.

	JMP	DEFADR			/IN CASE THE USER RESTARTS THE MACHINE.

	SLPSTRT				/*SLPSTRT

	RELOC	SLPSTRT			/WHERE THIS ASSEMBLES.

	JMP	SLIGO			/START OUR CODE AFTER WE'RE LOADED.

	RELOC				/TURN OFF RELOCATION.

	ZBLOCK	.&7600+200-.		/EMPTY SPACE.

	$				/THAT'S ALL FOLK!
